<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fan Ju</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 255 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Fan Sui</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fan Ju, also read Fan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a>, was a native of Wei who became chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> under King Zhaoxiang in 266 BCE. He advised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> to ally with distant states while attacking its neighbours, a strategy that guided its later conquests. His rivalry with the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bai-qi">Bai Qi</a> contributed to Bai Qi's forced suicide in 257 BCE.</p></div>
